This is the problem.
Without the E-word it is very difficult to survive with a weak
character like wizard.
But some techniques must be learnt.
Always write it before a baddie is near you. Then read it back to check
if it is correct.
Otherwise rewrite after clearing it.
When you have got it written once add another and read it back.
Remember that you cannot write more than 10 elbereths in one square
and 10 characters in a move.
Try to get two Elbereths on the square before you are really safe. As
one E-word can get destroyed in a single move. Always re-read it after
every move.
Reading it is not considered a move.
Also there are some safe things to do which will not rub it out any
faster than waiting.
Like searching. So when you are searching for a mimic always write the
E-word
and then do the search. You can do 10s and it will stop if the E-word
is gone in between.

Use the E-word correctly and it is much easier to survive.



